From: SingleAxis Fabric maintainers
Subject: [extension/bearertokenauth] add a fail-closed require_single_token mode

Since v0.151.0 the extension reads token files through the shared
credentials-file resolver. It trims the file, takes the first field of
each non-blank line, and keeps the last value when a reload fails or the
file becomes empty. That is the right default for a client credential,
but on a dedicated server ingress a deleted, emptied or malformed token
file leaves the previous credential accepted until a valid file appears.

Add an opt-in require_single_token mode for server-side source ingress.
It reads the raw file instead of the resolver and accepts exactly one
32-4096-byte printable ASCII token with no whitespace or newline; a
missing, unreadable or malformed file installs zero accepted tokens. It
reloads on any change in the file's parent directory (atomic renames and
projected Secret ..data swaps) and on a one-second poll, independent of
the Start context, so an unsafe rotation never leaves a stale credential
accepted. It requires filename without inline tokens and does not combine
with retry_on_failure or wait_for_token_file.

